    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 59 tests pass. **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI extended the business-day rule for the owner registration date to skip public holidays.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`, the `toBusinessDay(...)` method:\n\n- Previously it only rolled a Saturday/Sunday forward to the following Monday via a `switch` on the day of week.\n- Now it loops one day at a time while the date is a Saturday, Sunday, **or** a listed public holiday, so an adjusted date landing on a holiday rolls forward to the next non-holiday business day.\n- Added a `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS` constant with the fixed list: `2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28`. Note `2026-12-25` (Fri) \u2192 `2026-12-28` (Mon, also a holiday) \u2192 rolls on to `2026-12-29`, which the loop handles correctly.\n\nThis mirrors the reference `toBusinessDay`/`HOLIDAYS` already present in the test `AcceptanceBase`. The full suite (59 tests, including the new `Cp47Tests` holiday check) passes.",
